From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Backend: partner plans — prices, durations and the free trial as data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The partner price list was constants in three repositories: the day counts in
`src/utils/plan.util.js`, the prices in the website bundle, another copy in the
app — plus a literal `+ 20` for the free trial in `salonLogin.js`. A price change
meant a release of everything, and the copies had already drifted: the portal sold
₹199/₹299/₹499 with a 20-day trial, the app's renewal screen still showed the old
₹99/₹179/₹249 ladder, and this API granted a window neither screen described.

It is one table now, `partner_plans`, owned by the admin panel.

  · `partner_plans` — id (string, immutable: `salons.planType` stores it), label,
    price, days, note, badge, is_recommended, sort_order, is_active, is_free.
    Auto-loaded by `models/index.js` like every other model.
  · `ensurePlanSchema.js` — idempotent CREATE TABLE + `ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING`
    seed + index, called at boot beside `ensureShopBuyerSchema()`. Re-running it
    never resets a price an admin has changed.
  · Seeded exactly what was on sale before: `Free` 0/90 (the client's default
    trial), `monthly` 199/30, `trial_2_months` 299/60, `quarterly` 499/90.
  · `partnerPlan.service.js` — listPublic, listAdmin (per-plan salon counts plus
    the `orphaned` legacy ids), durationDays, defaultTrialDays, priceOf,
    assertPayableAmount, create, update, remove. Legacy `yearly` (365) and `FREE`
    (90) stay honoured so old subscriptions keep renewing; an unknown id is refused
    rather than silently defaulting.
  · `POST /api/salons/plans/list` — PUBLIC, registered above
    `salonRouter.use(authenticateAdmin)`: the registration screen shows prices
    before anyone has an account. Answers
    `{ data: { plans, freeTrial, currency, source } }`, falling back to the shipped
    catalog (`source: 'fallback'`) if the table cannot be read.
  · `POST /api/salons/admin/plans/{list,create,update,delete}` — admin only. Update
    keeps the id immutable; delete is refused while salons are on the plan unless
    `deactivate: true`, and the free trial can never be deleted.
  · Acceptance paths now read the table: `create-salon-with-plan` and
    `renew-salon-plan` take their duration from `durationDays(planType)` and — when
    a `totalAmount` is sent — refuse a payment that is not the stored price
    (±₹0.5) instead of charging it. `salonLogin.js` replaces the hard-coded
    `+ 20` with `defaultTrialDays()`.
  · `migrations/2026-11-05-partner-plans.sql` — schema, seed and the one data step
    this feature implies: a still-running free trial is extended to 90 days. Only
    free plans, only inside their original window; a paid plan is never touched and
    an expired trial is not resurrected. The previewing SELECT is in the file.

Verified on a fresh clone: `node --check` clean on all 14 files, the model
registers as `PartnerPlan → partner_plans` with exactly the migration's columns,
and — with the router mounted over a stub ORM — `POST /api/salons/plans/list`
answers 200 SUCCESS with no token while `POST /api/salons/admin/plans/list`
answers 401. The service was exercised end to end: create, price change, duration
change, delete refused while salons are on it, deactivate, second free plan
refused, unknown id refused, duplicate label refused, amount guard at ±₹0.5.
